{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Live validation of the fix — BOTH blocked closes now verify PASS\n\nRun from the fixed build (Gerrit 1700), read-only `rebar verify-completion`, no `--force`:\n\n- `wailsome-unsure-asianlion` (cb91-1535-fe3a-47fc) -> **PASS**, 4/4 criteria met, 0 findings.\n  Pre-fix this ticket failed three times: 3 unmet criteria citing `comments: []` / `status: open`\n  (both false against the store), then a bare FAIL naming no criterion at all.\n- `fixable-angular-caribou` (d4c2-b67e-ab99-4410) -> **PASS**, 5/5 criteria met, 0 findings,\n  metrics `requests=23 tool_calls=27 total_ms=108162`. Pre-fix it failed twice with \"Evidence\n  collection reached its search boundary\", and got WORSE (2 unmet -> 3) after evidence anchors\n  were added — because, as measured above, the pinned tree held 0 of its 13 comments, so the\n  anchors were invisible to the run they were written for. The completed 23-request search shows\n  the starvation was a symptom of searching for evidence the verifier had been told about but\n  could not read, not an inherently insufficient budget.\n\nTwo different presenting symptoms — \"the record does not exist\" and \"evidence collection reached\nits search boundary\" — one root cause. No step-budget change was needed for either.\n"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786592036883686001,"uuid":"134a6ebc-3c7c-4860-8a96-280007ace7f8"}